          "text": "The original method stops at any NUL or space after the digits, ignoring invalid bytes that follow. It also fails to enforce the minimum length and required trailing terminator, and reports the wrong position for invalid bytes.\n\n```java\npublic static long parseOctal(final byte[] buffer, final int offset,\n        final int length) {\n    if (length < 2) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException(\n                \"Length \" + length + \" must be at least 2\");\n    }\n\n    long result = 0L;\n    int start = offset;\n    int end = offset + length;\n\n    // Missing fields consisting entirely of NULs are valid.\n    boolean allNuls = true;\n    for (int i = start; i < end; i++) {\n        if (buffer[i] != 0) {\n            allNuls = false;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    if (allNuls) {\n        return 0L;\n    }\n\n    // Require one trailing NUL or space.\n    byte currentByte = buffer[end - 1];\n    if (currentByte != 0 && currentByte != (byte) ' ') {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException(\n                exceptionMessage(buffer, offset, length, end - 1, currentByte));\n    }\n    end--;\n\n    // Allow one additional trailing NUL or space.\n    if (end > start) {\n        currentByte = buffer[end - 1];\n        if (currentByte == 0 || currentByte == (byte) ' ') {\n            end--;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Skip leading spaces, but validate every remaining byte.\n    while (start < end && buffer[start] == (byte) ' ') {\n        start++;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = start; i < end; i++) {\n        currentByte = buffer[i];\n        if (currentByte < '0' || currentByte > '7') {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\n                    exceptionMessage(buffer, offset, length, i, currentByte));\n        }\n        result = (result << 3) + (currentByte - '0');\n    }\n\n    return result;\n}\n```"
